  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A proton, a neutron, an electron and an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-particle have same energy. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math> are the de Broglie&#39;s wavelengths of proton, neutron, electron and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;particle respectively, then choose the correct relation from the following&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NJs3M",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eIGev",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cNndb",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IfVBf",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math>.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The de-Broglie wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>)</mo></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;constant</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Mass of the particle</p><p>Thus, with increasing mass of particle de-Broglie wavelength decreases.</p><p>Order of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math></p><p>Order of de-Broglie wavelength is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
